    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0160" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 832.73/111</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-13T17:00:00-03:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President of Brazil and Minister of Public Works have signed concession giving
                    Central &amp; South American Telegraph Co. right <pb facs="0161" n="49"
                        xml:id="pg49"/> to lay submarine cables as desired. This assures us cable
                    communication between the United States and Brazil over an all-American line and
                    breaks British monopoly. Decree will be published shortly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
